target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheLabelMovesEvenWhenTheCommentFails'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the Python's `if a.label:` sits AFTER both the posted and the comment-failed branches, so it runs whenever a PR number is known, and nothing about `gh pr edit` depends on the comment having landed. Returning early instead dropped the at-a-glance signal for exactly the runs whose report is hardest to find — the ones whose comment failed and whose body is now only in `.git/info`. Found independently by three agents in separate contexts during the slice's own review.
--- old
		if p.Label {
			applyLabel(p, probe.Number, diag)
		}
		return path, nil
	}
--- new
		return path, nil
	}
